{"type":"message","id":"9a4140f8","parentId":"7b12f4f8","timestamp":"2026-03-13T18:21:11.978Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\nGot it, let's tackle this task. First, I need to search the skills directory for files related to markdown to word/office/doc/docx conversion. First step: list all the directories in /home/yankeeting/.openclaw/workspace/skills first? Wait no, better to use grep to search for keywords in all SKILL.md files under that directory, right? Because each skill has a SKILL.md. Let's use exec to run a find command combined with grep. The command should find all SKILL.md files under the skills dir, then search for keywords like markdown, word, doc, docx, office, convert, 转换, etc. Let's write that command:\n\nfind /home/yankeeting/.openclaw/workspace/skills -name \"SKILL.md\" -type f | xargs grep -lE \"(markdown|md).*(word|office|doc|docx|转换)|(word|office|doc|docx|转换).*(markdown|md)\" 2>/dev/null\n\nWait yeah, that should find all SKILL.md files that mention both markdown (or md) and word/doc/docx/office/转换 related to conversion. Then once I get the list of files, I can read each one to get their path and core functionality.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_el22zbkw40oumctmr6zg8bp7","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /home/yankeeting/.openclaw/workspace/skills -name \"SKILL.md\" -type f | xargs grep -lE \"(markdown|md).*(word|office|doc|docx|转换)|(word|office|doc|docx|转换).*(markdown|md)\" 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"volces-com","model":"ark-code-latest","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773426066446}}
